/*  showGen -- GX-6, THE LOOKSEE. Run it and read the generated parse method.

    NO PREPARATION: no environment variable, no shell, no arguments. Open it in
    Xcode, run, read the output. The capture arms itself with recordParse()
    below, which is the in-fixture door onto the same gate INCANT_PARSE_RECORD
    opens.

    TO LOOK AT A DIFFERENT RULE, EDIT THE TWO MARKED LINES AT THE FOOT --
    and it is two, not one, which is worth saying plainly. Incant fixtures are
    invoked as `incant <file>` with no argument channel, so the name cannot be
    passed in. Naming it ONCE in a field and using it twice was tried first and
    DOES NOT WORK: `genParse(gsRule)` resolves nothing and prints nothing, at
    exit 0. Both call sites need the quoted literal, so they are kept adjacent
    and marked to make a half-edit obvious at a glance.

    GENERATION ONLY. This does not install anything, does not touch
    incant/grammar, and cannot move a baseline: genParse emits and installs
    nothing (its own header says so), and the ParsE record is gated. Fleet
    neutral by construction.

    The twelve plannable rules are: Braced Parens ElsE InvokE InvokeArg
    PrintField WardeD GrouP CodE RunRulE BlocK ExpressioN.  */
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;
registry(cOMMANDs);
define genParse immediateAction=genParse; ;
define showParse immediateAction=showParse; ;
define recordParse immediateAction=recordParse; ;
recordParse();
print "---- generated method ----":;
/*  <<<< EDIT BOTH OF THESE -- same rule name, quoted >>>>  */
genParse('Parens');
showParse('Parens');
/*  <<<< end of the edit >>>>  */
print "SHOWGEN SENTINEL":;
stop();
